I challenge catalogue row [69fe684bf76585e8] which claims the grounding kernel does not move under upper-case. The row's example likely has span and document that match verbatim regardless of case. My input has a span in lowercase that occurs in the document only when case is ignored. The upper-case transform converts the entire reply to capitals, making the span match verbatim in the document after transformation. Before the transform, _span_occurs with empty relaxations returns NOT_IN_DOCUMENT because 'hello' does not occur verbatim in 'HELLO world' after whitespace normalization. After the transform, both become uppercase and 'HELLO' occurs verbatim in 'HELLO WORLD', returning 'verbatim'. This refutes the 'moves: false' claim.
commitments: {"kernel": "conformance.kernel.grounding", "transform": "conformance.transform.upper-case", "input": "{\"span\": \"hello\", \"document\": \"HELLO world\"}"}
